or your own life  [Music]  the bottom line is don't die and we say  this every day to ourselves  to our children to our parents to our  loved ones our friends and even everyone  that we see in hardship a hurricane the  fires the wildfires in california we got  i hope no one dies  in the wars around the world  in the ill areas of illness and  especially covid19 where people have  less medical care and are  very densely populated we go hope they  don't die  so it's a natural instinctive desire  that we don't die however if it's a  foregone conclusion then why does time  matter does it matter if you die at five  or 95  so that we put  value on someone's worth age worth  rather than their merit worth or their  love worth we usually consider someone  young to be more important than someone  old  so let's change that mode of thinking  too  the reason why in my view that we've  invested so much in this narrative this  historical lore that travels across  centuries and cultures  so it's not geographical and it's not  age related it's a timeless notion  civilization has invested  in this need for death to tell their  stories  life is not meaningful without death  the old should die and make way for the  young  you've outworn your stay overpopulation  global warming  we tend to start placing the emphasis on  our deficits our problems based on too  many people older people  disrespected people  those in grades  our biases our prejudice also come into  this equation  we spend more time more money and more  effort  on  continuing this narrative then  addressing the problem so then the  question is what's the problem the  problem is disease and aging  the battle against aging and disease and  the finality or the foregone conclusion  of death  wages on regardless of the advances in  science the advances in technology and  the minds of people  [Music]  that are historical the genius mind of  each person and those who we say are  genius who the inventors who create  marvelous  opportunities have yet to solve this  problem have yet  to end this war  so i'm introducing now my life portfolio  it's about smart investing not just in  your livelihood but in yourself and i  think the greatest investment we can do  is in ourselves to make our lives  meaningful purposeful  and to share to be  benevolent  to be generous  and importantly to share our knowledge  with others  the accumulation of human knowledge is  worth sharing and so we need to invest  in the information  not the misinformation and we'll get  into a little bit of why i think  investing in information is so important  so now we approach how how we're going  to do this  how is always a good question so how  with a portfolio strategy i've broken it  down into three specific areas the  conservative investment in your life  your prolongation your preservation of  your life staying alive  the moderate growth  and the high risk aggressive investment  we'll take a look at this and it's i've  created a bit of a  play on your portfolio investment and  finances but there is no greater  investment than your life so  here  diversity is essential  so what does this portfolio look like  i call it the super longevity portfolio  and you'll see i have three different  quadrants here the conservative the  moderate growth and the high risk  aggressive growth  i've broken it down into chronological  age and i'm someone who  is not an ageist and i don't even like  quantifying or qualifying a person based  on their age but because we live in a  world that is time-based age is  important when we're thinking about our  lifespan because as we age we are more  prone to certain diseases  and if we want to answer the question  how to live forever then we need to  consider this  okay so let's look at the first quadrant  i have the ages 20 to 40. that's when we  start thinking about  our aging usually we don't think about  it prior to that unless you have a  disease and illness or an injury but  let's just go to the mainstream area  here 75  of our investment should be in  eating exercising the healthy things  that we do um  getting enough sleep not partying too  much certainly not drinking too much or  doing too many drugs but staying healthy  and that largely is  eating well kato diet or maybe a little  bit of calorie restriction but being  aware that  we need a certain amount of protein we  need our vegetables of course and we  need our fats so that is based on your  personal um  biological system and what your needs  are you may have allergies to things but  basically that that very conservative is  doing the basic things to live as long  as possible as healthfully as possible  to get to that maximum lifespan of 122  to 123 years approximately that's our  shelf life  so  you want to take care of your body but  also your brain and the brain is still  very plastic at this time the plasticity  the learning the acquiring of  information  is really good so this is a low-risk  strategy  and it's a fixed genomic portfolio  so this would be for the younger  generation when we get into the  chronological age of middle age say 40  to 70 somewhere within that spectrum we  want to take a little bit more risk and  it's moderate growth  the primary goal of this law longevity  is not to die so  we want to generate  current information on all the  breakthroughs and there's breakthroughs  going on on a daily basis and gene  therapies genomics  biotechnologies nanomedicine stem cells  looking at reversing aging the the  telomeres and the enzyme the telomerase  what causes aging looking at hormones  our peptides our proteins  our whole cellular system and with that  information now this is really important  in the moderate growth portfolio  that you gain information you absorb  information you do the moderate  you have  20 in the moderate you've already  maintained your healthfulness by this  time by eating well getting enough sleep  reducing stress  those basic fundamental needs for your  mind and body but here we're going to  gather information because you don't  want to take too much risk and i'll  explain that in a moment to continue  watching this video click the link in  the top left or in the description below  or visit iai.tv for more debates and  talks from the world's leading thinkers  on today's biggest ideas  you

